{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review consumer rights protections for vehicles supplied via salary sacrifice",
        "additional_details": "Salary sacrifice schemes lack the same consumer rights available to private lease customers as contracts are between employers and vehicle providers. Employees can be left paying for defective or unsafe vehicles, particularly EVs, despite repeated faults, lengthy repair delays and limited rights of rejection. We ask the Government to investigate how these arrangements might circumvent the Consumer Rights Act 2015 and to ensure employees retain rejection, replacement and termination rights without penalty.",
        "background": "Review consumer protection laws for salary sacrifice vehicles, particularly EV's. Ensure employees have enforceable rights to reject unsafe or defective vehicles, obtain timely repairs or replacements, and terminate agreements without financial penalty where serious faults remain unresolved.",
